why A rare off-hand for your 50s from Niby and Impsy in Felwood, the camp that also offers An Imp's Request.

# Niby the Almighty's errands in Felwood: What Niby Commands (7601) to Impsy,
# Flawless Fel Essence (7602: Azshara, Jaedenar and the Dark Portal) and
# Kroshius' Infernal Core (7603), for the Shard of the Green Flame.
# Drops (items.json): each essence three times in four from its mobs: Legashi
# Satyrs, Rogues and Hellcallers (51-53, Azshara), Jaedenar Legionnaires (55),
# Felguard Sentries (54, Blasted Lands); none elite. Player notes report few
# spawns and long waits for the last two. The same Legashi and Felguards drop
# Felcloth for Impsy's own chain (forever/class/warlock/impsys-request).
# Kroshius (55) is elite and immune to fire; he wakes only when the Fel Fire
# (given at the accept) is used at his remains. Lost Fel Fire: abandon and
# take the quest again (player reports).
# ASSUMED: The chain runs as in Classic (Classic flow; Forever's data has no play reports past the level-30 beta cap). In-game check: Kroshius wakes at the Fel Fire and the essences drop as listed.
# Sources: Forever's quest data (quests.json, npcs.json, items.json); the
# quest notes (data/local/mechanics) for the camps and the fight; the
# reference class guides for the order.

step Niby the Almighty
  tip At 50 Niby the Almighty and his imp Impsy wait on a rise in central Felwood just north-east of Bloodvenom Post: coming north over the Bloodvenom Falls bridge, they stand off the road to the east, past a few oozes. Niby sends you to Impsy, beside him, who wants three Flawless Fel Essences from three places.
  level 50
  accept 7601                         -- Niby the Almighty
  turnin 7601                         -- Impsy
  accept 7602

step Jaedenar
  tip Jaedenar lies just south of Bloodvenom Post, west of the road. Of its two caves, Shadow Hold is the northern one, further up the hill; the other has no Legionnaires. Shadow Hold's tunnels run north under the hills, and the Jaedenar Legionnaires (level 55) stand in its deeper halls, from the first ramps on toward Lord Banehollow's chamber; they Uppercut anyone in melee. Three kills in four give the essence, but only about eleven spawn: clear your way in and wait out a five-minute respawn if you must. The cultists of Jaedenar and Shadow Hold are all hostile.
  collect 18622 quest 7602.2          -- Flawless Fel Essence (Jaedenar)

step Azshara
  zone Azshara
  tip The Legashi satyrs (level 51-53) hold the Legash Encampment on Azshara's northern coast. Every kind drops the essence three times in four; the satyrs burn mana and the Hellcallers rain fire, so pull them singly.
  collect 18624 quest 7602.1          -- Flawless Fel Essence (Azshara)

step The Dark Portal
  zone Blasted Lands
  tip The Felguard Sentries (level 54) walk around the Dark Portal in the south of the Blasted Lands, each with a felhunter. Leave the level 57 Servants of Razelikh alone: they cannot be killed without their own quest.
  collect 18623 quest 7602.3          -- Flawless Fel Essence (Dark Portal)

step Impsy
  zone Felwood
  tip Back to Impsy. He hands you the Fel Fire: keep it, it wakes the infernal Kroshius.
  turnin 7602                         -- Impsy
  accept 7603

step Kroshius
  tip Kroshius' remains lie in Shatter Scar Vale, the burnt crater north of Niby: follow the road north from his camp; the remains lie a little east of it. Use the Fel Fire beside them and wait for him to rise. Kroshius is elite (level 55): grouping up is encouraged; a warlock of 55 or more can solo him with Fear and damage over time, or with Enslave Demon, but fire spells do nothing to him and he knocks you back. If you die he heals to full; he rises again three minutes after he dies. An elite infernal patrols the pool south of the remains: pull Kroshius away from it. He always drops his core. Lost the Fel Fire? Abandon the quest and take it again from Impsy.
  use 18626 @45.7,34.8                -- Fel Fire, at Kroshius' Remains
  kill 14467 quest 7603.1             -- Kroshius
  collect 18625 quest 7603.2          -- Kroshius' Infernal Core

step Back to Niby
  turnin 7603                         -- Niby the Almighty: Shard of the Green Flame
